Note that system shock is not an instakill.  Instead it causes damage,
and only kills if the player runs out of hit points in the process.
Thus having more than 30 hit points is a failsafe protection against
system shock.  The play also won't die if the random damage is less
than his remaining HP, or if he succeeds from the constitution check,
or is a dragon, werething or vampire.  (Or has "forcecontrol," but I
don't know what that is.)

